.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-config-diff 1  "rev-stealth-config-diff " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-config\-diff \- Print a unified diff between the live `<path>` and the in\-repo `templates/policy.toml` baseline. Headers use `\-\-\-` / `+++`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth config diff\fR [\fB\-\-against\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a unified diff between the live <path> and a baseline (default: in\-repo templates/policy.toml). Headers use `\-\-\-` / `+++` so the output drops cleanly into `patch`.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-against\fR \fI<AGAINST>\fR
Override the baseline (defaults to `templates/policy.toml`)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Path to the live config file (e.g. `~/.rev_scraping/policy.toml`)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth config diff ~/.rev_scraping/policy.toml
  $ rev\-stealth config diff ~/.rev_scraping/policy.toml \-\-against ./templates/policy.toml

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Diff emitted (no change is still exit 0).
  1  UserError        Bad <path>.
  3  PermanentError   IO failure.

ENV:
  (none consumed directly; baseline path resolves via the binary\*(Aqs compile\-time root.)
